===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} A very [[rapid]]ly moving object, especially one that is [[throw]]n.
#: '' The pitcher threw a real '''zinger''' and struck him out. ''
# {{lb|en|informal}} A [[surprising]] or unusually [[pointed]], humorous and impressive insult.
#* {{quote-book|year=2007|title=Seasons in Time  |author= Larry Groves |page=112 |ISBN=1465328815 |passage=I wasn't looking to make friends; there had been too much animosity between us in the past, and maybe the guy had a '''zinger''' waiting on me. }}
#: ''My little niece let fly with the '''zinger''' that my sister was pregnant again.''
# {{lb|en|informal}} An event that when experienced leaves the witness [[daze]]d, either physically or metaphorically.
#: '' I was still reeling from the '''zinger''' of seeing my ex on a date with my best friend. ''
# {{lb|en|informal}} An outstanding, energetic and surprising thing or person.

